  "interpretation": [
    "DRAGREF residuals are now confirmed to be genuine legacy DRAGREF outputs. They fall from +2.67 Mm at 65 km to +0.344 Mm at 50 km, then +0.281 Mm at 45 km and +0.168 Mm immediately before the runway-longitude pass.",
    "At the first runway-longitude passage the vehicle was about 39.8 km high, Mach 5.37, and 1.78 km/s; it continued about 217 km of recorded ground path before the archive ended without TAEM. The scalar DRAGREF path estimate is not a target-capture predictor: the 45 km state had about 291 km predicted range while the vehicle subsequently flew about 323 km and still did not acquire TAEM.",
    "After passage, measured banked lift closely matches the lateral acceleration needed for the trajectory the vehicle actually flew at +55 s and +90 s. At +90 s it was about 129 km from the runway, nearly 175\u00b0 off the runway bearing, and would need about 33 m/s\u00b2 average lateral acceleration to turn through that angle within the remaining great-circle range; the same measured lift at the configured 70\u00b0 bank gives only about 5.9 m/s\u00b2. This diagnostic assumes current lift remains representative and does not prove the absolute aerodynamic/control maximum.",
    "The failure evidence favors early route capture and lead-in curvature over further scalar L/D tuning. It does not authorize changing the shadow gate or low-q bank ramp; the archived flight bypassed qualification and does not isolate the responsible control-axis sign or coordination."
  ],
